  "circulation": "Formal loop runs through foyer, drawing room and library. Separate kitchen/service loop reaches ballroom without crossing the grand stair. Attic is a deliberate terminal search with warning at the upper servants passage; retreat via that passage and grand gallery.",
  "systems": "Reception, service and upper suites have separate circuits. Tall ballroom carries sound differently from bookshelves and low attic rafters; greenhouse and garden have exposed weather baselines.",
  "campaign": "Estate correspondence introduces suppliers and family patrons. Optional attic archive revisits use the same reserved geometry; no hidden story room is required for a legal rite.",
  "refine": [
    "Grand stair requires a two-flight return and real gallery void; upper gallery rectangle is a planning envelope around that void.",
    "Draw attic headroom under roof slopes before placing the 4.4 m ritual square.",
    "Compare with approved mansion board; refine servants access and door apertures before replacing the cross-wing prototype."
  ],
